{"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Matula–Beck: repeatedly remove a vertex of least degree in what is left (the least index on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ties), then colour in the reverse of that removal order. At most degeneracy + 1 colours, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"at most 6 on a planar graph. O((n + m) log n)."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"smallestLast","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/coloringstrategy\/smallestlast"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"case","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"smallestLast"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"Coloring.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/ColoringModule\/Coloring.swift#L116"},"modules":[{"name":"ColoringModule"}],"roleHeading":"Case","externalID":"s:14ColoringModule0A8StrategyO12smallestLastyA2CmF","title":"ColoringStrategy.smallestLast"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/smallestLast","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/ColoringStrategy/smallestLast":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/smallestLast","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/coloringstrategy\/smallestlast","kind":"symbol","title":"ColoringStrategy.smallestLast","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"smallestLast"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Matula–Beck: repeatedly remove a vertex of least degree in what is left (the least index on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ties), then colour in the reverse of that removal order. At most degeneracy + 1 colours, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"at most 6 on a planar graph. O((n + m) log n)."}]},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule","kind":"symbol","title":"ColoringModule","role":"collection","abstract":[]},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/ColoringStrategy":{"title":"ColoringStrategy","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ColoringStrategy"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How "},{"code":"greedyColoring(strategy:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" orders the vertices. Each vertex in turn takes the least colour"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"none of its already coloured neighbours has (first fit). Degrees are simple degrees (distinct"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other neighbours, self-loops left out); ties go to the lesser vertex index, except for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":".coloredNeighbors","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ColoringStrategy"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/coloringstrategy"}}}